exercises.solution:
```python
def negation(u, opens):
    best = frozenset()
    for w in opens:
        if not (w & u):
            best = best | w
    return best


def is_boolean(opens, top):
    return all(u | negation(u, opens) == top for u in opens)
```

The union of all opens disjoint from $u$ is open and disjoint from $u$, so it is the largest such — that is $\neg u = u \Rightarrow 0$. For the Sierpiński truth values $\varnothing \subset \{0\} \subset \{0, 1\}$ we get $\neg\{0\} = \varnothing$, so $\{0\} \cup \neg\{0\} \neq \{0, 1\}$: not Boolean. For a discrete poset every subset is a down-set and negation is set complement.
